## Instruction
The `WatchItem` interface imported from './movie' now names the flag `seen` instead of `watched` (required boolean, otherwise identical: { id: number; title: string; seen: boolean; poster_path?: string | null; release_date?: string; }). Update every place the store touches that field: `add()` must create the new item with `seen: false`; `toggleWatched(id)` must flip the item's `seen` value; `watchedCount` must count items with `seen === true`; and any JSON persisted to localStorage must store the flag under the `seen` key (no migration of previously persisted `watched` data is required). All exported names and signatures stay exactly as they are (`items`, `count`, `watchedCount`, `add`, `remove`, `toggleWatched`) - method and signal names are not fields and must not be renamed. If existing tests in watchlist-store.spec.ts reference the old `watched` field, make the source change anyway and request the test change.

